 ## Acceptance criteria
 
-- [ ] *"solo 30 minuti oggi"* reaches an adaptation; accepted, the mesocycle in the database is unchanged.
-- [ ] *"basta affondi"* reaches a change; accepted, the new mesocycle has no lunges and continues the cycle count.
-- [ ] A sentence that could be either is asked about, not guessed.
-- [ ] Full test suite and mypy green.
+- [x] *"solo 30 minuti oggi"* reaches an adaptation; accepted, the mesocycle in the database is unchanged. (Scripted entrance.)
+- [x] *"basta affondi"* reaches a change; accepted, the new mesocycle has no lunges and continues the cycle count. (Scripted entrance.)
+- [ ] A sentence that could be either is asked about, not guessed. The prompt says so and a question back starts nothing (scripted); the reading on a real entrance model is not measured.
+- [x] Full test suite and mypy green: 1550, mypy clean.
+
+## Comments
+
+- `adapt_today(minutes, without)` is the one handoff with arguments: today's constraint as data, so the validator holds the plan to it. `without` is checked against `training.toml`'s equipment. `change_mesocycle` takes none; the user's words reach the planner verbatim either way.
+- A change keeps the replaced mesocycle's `cycles` and `accepted_after`; the validator refuses a different `cycles`. Both an adaptation and a change withdraw today's unperformed serving, so asking again serves the new one.
+- `trainer plan --time/--equipment/--exclude/--avoid` adapts when a mesocycle serves today and plans from nothing otherwise; `trainer plan --change WORDS` is the CLI's change.
+- Not closed: the workspace is not a git repository (no commit, no hash), no provider was reachable for the real-model reading, and `/code-review` was not run.
